# Frontend conventions

React 19, Vite 8, TypeScript, built to `static/spa/` and served by Flask. Same stack as
`nvis-rack-status`, so patterns transfer.

## Styling: Kaizen first, MUI second, custom last

Load order in `main.tsx` matters and is not arbitrary:

```typescript
import "./styles/kaizen/base.css";
import "./styles/kaizen/components.css";
import "./index.css";
```

Kaizen UI Foundations CSS is **vendored** under `src/styles/kaizen/` rather than fetched from a CDN,
so the build works air-gapped. If you refresh it from upstream, re-apply the font URL rewrite from
the CDN path to `./fonts/`.

Reach for a Kaizen class before an MUI component, and an MUI component before writing CSS. The
NVIDIA green (`#76B900`) lives in `theme.ts`; do not hardcode it anywhere else.

**Text sizing has its own rule: @frontend-typography.mdc.** Read it before you set a size. Which
Kaizen step goes where is measured rather than guessed, and the failure modes are unintuitive
enough that three separate attempts to fix them here made the problem worse.

## Routing

`HashRouter`, not `BrowserRouter`. The SPA is served by Flask from a static directory, and hash
routes mean no server-side route configuration and no 404 on refresh.

## Talking to the backend

All requests go through `src/lib/apiFetch.ts`. It uses same-origin relative URLs with
`credentials: "same-origin"` — there is no CORS in production, by design — and it handles the
401-then-refresh dance in one place.

Domain calls live in `src/services/*.ts` and return parsed types, not `Response` objects. A
component should never see `{ok: false}`; the service turns that into a thrown error.

## State

React Context, no Redux or Zustand. Providers live in `src/context/`. If a piece of state is only
used by one subtree, it does not need a provider.

## Long-running assessments

An assessment run takes minutes and streams progress. Views subscribe rather than poll where
possible, and **must** render the intermediate states honestly — a run that is waiting on the LLM
says so. Never show a spinner that implies work is happening when the run has actually failed and
is awaiting retry.
